From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: suniv: let the VE clock set its PLL rate

The VE module clock is a bare gate on pll-ve, so cedrus' clk_set_rate()
of its suniv mod_rate (297 MHz) never reaches the PLL and the engine runs
at the PLL_VE reset default of 210 MHz. pll-ve has no other consumer on
this SoC; propagate the rate like the H3 CCU does. The manual specifies
PLL_VE for 30-600 MHz and rates the VE for H.264 1080p30.

Measured at 210 MHz with an 800x480 CarPlay stream: 10 ms per frame at
rest, 18-21 ms during fast scrolling -- below the 60 fps the phone sends.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-suniv-f1c100s.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-suniv-f1c100s.c
@@ -311,7 +311,8 @@
  * TODO: BSP says the parent is pll-audio, however common sense and experience
  * told us it should be pll-ve. pll-ve is totally not used in BSP code.
  */
-static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(ve_clk, "ve", "pll-ve", 0x13c, BIT(31), 0);
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(ve_clk, "ve", "pll-ve", 0x13c, BIT(31),
+		      CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
 
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(codec_clk, "codec", "pll-audio", 0x140, BIT(31),
 		      CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
